<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ariarathid dynasty</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ariarathid dynasty ruled Cappadocia in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> from the late 4th century BCE until about 96 BCE. Of Persian origin, its kings, most of them named Ariarathes, mixed Iranian traditions with Greek culture and allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> from the 2nd century BCE. When the line died out amid interference by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mithridates-vi-of-pontus">Mithridates VI of Pontus</a>, Rome approved Ariobarzanes I as king.</p></div>
